            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-49083-cryptography",
              "name": "PythonMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-49083 high vulnerability for cryptography package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "cryptography is a package designed to expose cryptographic primitives and recipes to Python developers. Calling `load_pem_pkcs7_certificates` or `load_der_pkcs7_certificates` could lead to a NULL-pointer dereference and segfault. Exploitation of this vulnerability poses a serious risk of Denial of Service (DoS) for any application attempting to deserialize a PKCS7 blob/certificate. The consequences extend to potential disruptions in system availability and stability. This vulnerability has been patched in version 41.0.6."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-49083",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-49083\nSeverity: high\nPackage: cryptography\nVersion: 3.2\nFix Version: 41.0.6\nType: python\nLocation: /lab5-canary/requirements.txt\nData Namespace: nvd:language:python\nLink: [CVE-2023-49083](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-49083)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-49083**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | cryptography  | 3.2  | 41.0.6  | python  | /lab5-canary/requirements.txt  | nvd:language:python  | [CVE-2023-49083](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-49083)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:pypi/cryptography@3.2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-23931-cryptography",
              "name": "PythonMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-23931 medium vulnerability for cryptography package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "cryptography is a package designed to expose cryptographic primitives and recipes to Python developers. In affected versions `Cipher.update_into` would accept Python objects which implement the buffer protocol, but provide only immutable buffers. This would allow immutable objects (such as `bytes`) to be mutated, thus violating fundamental rules of Python and resulting in corrupted output. This now correctly raises an exception. This issue has been present since `update_into` was originally introduced in cryptography 1.8."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-23931",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-23931\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: cryptography\nVersion: 3.2\nFix Version: 39.0.1\nType: python\nLocation: /lab5-canary/requirements.txt\nData Namespace: nvd:language:python\nLink: [CVE-2023-23931](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-23931)",
